From: Port-SotC-Mobile capture-host patches
Subject: [PATCH] non-Vita build fixes for game overrides at celosia f8c269e

Two latent bugs that only manifest when PS2X_VU_NEON_A32 == 0 (every
non-Vita host: macOS ARM, Linux x86_64, Android ARM64). The Vita
(ARMv7 + USE_SSE2NEON) path compiles around both, which is why upstream
did not see them; the commit's own message (r122 Vita3K measurement)
shows the active target is the Vita.

1. game/overrides/coll125.h: coll125::clip() redeclared 'const __m128
   vf0c' in the same scope (once in the #else branch of
   #if PS2X_VU_NEON_A32, once after the #endif). Renamed the second
   occurrence to vf0u (identical value, single user in the dot lambda).

2. game/overrides/decomp_collision.cpp: keepFastOk() called
   fast::check49(), but namespace fast (check49 included) is entirely
   inside the #if PS2X_VU_NEON_A32 block. keepFastOk now returns false
   on non-Vita, matching keepEarlyAt()'s own #else (the round 119 fast
   path is off there anyway).

Both verified by compiling decomp_collision.cpp standalone with the
exact ps2EntryRunner unity-batch command line (x86_64 GCC 15, -msse4.1,
SIMDe NEON shim per D13, mach-o shim per D16).
---
diff --git a/game/overrides/coll125.h b/game/overrides/coll125.h
index 9524f38..8e6d109 100644
--- a/game/overrides/coll125.h
+++ b/game/overrides/coll125.h
@@ -448,12 +448,12 @@ namespace coll125
                 return 0;
         }
         // u / v: the triangle's terms made once (triangleTerms), the crossing's side here, as ClipCollisionDB
-        const __m128 vf0c = vu::clamp(vf0);
+        const __m128 vf0u = vu::clamp(vf0);
         const __m128 w = vu::clamp(PS2_VSUB(p, e.v0));
         auto dot = [&](__m128 a, __m128 b)
         {
             const __m128 prod = vu::mulN(a, b);
-            __m128 acc = vu::addN(vf0c, lane<0>(prod));
+            __m128 acc = vu::addN(vf0u, lane<0>(prod));
             acc = vu::addN(acc, lane<1>(prod));
             return x(vu::addN(acc, lane<2>(prod)));
         };
diff --git a/game/overrides/decomp_collision.cpp b/game/overrides/decomp_collision.cpp
index 4e092b0..c06989a 100644
--- a/game/overrides/decomp_collision.cpp
+++ b/game/overrides/decomp_collision.cpp
@@ -1349,7 +1349,13 @@ namespace decomp_collision
         return false;
 #endif
     }
+#if PS2X_VU_NEON_A32
     inline bool keepFastOk() { return sotc_decomp::fastNativeOn() && !fast::check49(); }
+#else
+    // fast::check49 (round 49's NEON fast-path checks) is Vita-only; the round
+    // 119 fast path is off here (keepEarlyAt above returns false the same way).
+    inline bool keepFastOk() { return false; }
+#endif
     // The same for the surface id at `id` (the chain made here).
     bool keepEarly(uint8_t *rdram, R5900Context *ctx, PS2Runtime *runtime, uint32_t id, uint32_t point, float keep)
     {
